# Q4. Starvation Debugging

## Problem

Scheduler:

Q1 → Interactive

Q2 → System

Q3 → Batch

P5 is in Q3.

---

## Root Cause

Higher-priority queues continuously receive new jobs.

Q3 receives CPU only when Q1 and Q2 become empty.

Since this rarely happens, P5 waits indefinitely.

This is starvation.

---

## Optimization

Implement Aging.

Example:

Every 30 seconds

Increase process priority.

Eventually P5 moves to Q2 and later Q1.

---

## Benefits

- Prevents starvation
- Ensures fairness
- Improves response time

---

## Conclusion

Aging gradually increases waiting process priority and guarantees CPU allocation.
